# tleap assembly for the MOR-ZH853 membrane system.  ***TEMPLATE -- do not run directly.***
# ff19SB protein + Lipid21 membrane + OPC water + GAFF2/RESP ligand (SPECIFICATION D-12).
#
# make_tleap.py reads the packed system and substitutes @PLACEHOLDERS@ to produce tleap_run.in,
# which is what 01_build_system.sh actually feeds to tleap. Two things cannot be hardcoded here:
#   @DISULFIDES@ -- loadpdb renumbers every residue sequentially from 1 across the WHOLE system
#                   (protein, then lipids, then water), so the OPRM1 numbering is gone by the time
#                   `bond` runs. C142/C219 happen to be 74/151 for the current 69-349 construct,
#                   but that shifts with ACE/NME caps or any change of construct boundaries.
#   @SETBOX@     -- the box must be the periodic cell PACKMOL packed into. `setBox sys vdw` derives
#                   a box from van der Waals extents instead, which does not reproduce the packing
#                   cell and leaves the system wrong at the periodic boundary.
source leaprc.protein.ff19SB
source leaprc.lipid21
source leaprc.water.opc
source leaprc.gaff2

#   @LIGAND_PARAMS@ -- the loadmol2/loadamberparams pair for whichever ligand is being built,
#                      or a comment for an apo build. The unit MUST be named LIG: loadpdb matches
#                      the packed residue to a unit BY NAME, and fix_ligand.py renames the packed
#                      ligand (deposited name L01) to LIG for exactly that reason.
@LIGAND_PARAMS@

# assembled, pre-packed, pre-solvated system from PACKMOL-Memgen, with disulfide cysteines
# renamed CYS -> CYX by make_tleap.py so ff19SB does not add an HG to a bonded sulfur.
sys = loadpdb @SYSTEM_PDB@

# conserved disulfide (human OPRM1 C142-C219), in tleap's sequential numbering
@DISULFIDES@

# NOTE: cap truncated receptor termini (T69/F349) with ACE/NME before this step,
# and set HIS tautomers + D2.50 (ASH116 for the protonated variant) in the input PDB.

@SETBOX@
check sys
saveamberparm sys system.prmtop system.rst7
quit
